<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="014" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Teams personal-tab manifest + CSP frame-ancestors + Teams theme bridging</title>
    <phase>P1 Module-host foundation</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:011</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New-file creation (manifest, staticwebapp.config.json CSP) + theme-bridge wiring; not core .cs/auth logic; STANDARD per CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Config + manifest authoring against a proven teams-app-r1 recipe — literal execution.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>After 011 lands, runs in parallel-group B with 012/017; touches manifest + SWA config + theme bridge, not the shared frame that 013 edits.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011</deps>
    <tags>frontend, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Package the same SWA as a Teams personal-tab app: author the Teams manifest, set staticwebapp.config.json
    CSP frame-ancestors to allow Teams origins (no X-Frame-Options), and bridge the Teams theme (light/dark/
    high-contrast) into the Fluent v9 provider. Build on the teams-app-r1 prior art; do not rebuild host detection.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Teams personal-tab + SWA hosting + Fluent v9 theming specialist.</role>

  <goal>
    A Teams personal-tab manifest pointing at the SWA content URL; staticwebapp.config.json CSP
    frame-ancestors 'self' https://teams.microsoft.com https://*.cloud.microsoft with no X-Frame-Options;
    a Teams theme bridge that maps Teams light/dark/contrast to the Fluent v9 theme. The app loads and renders
    correctly inside Teams (including dark) framed by Teams.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec FR-04 + design.md F4 + ux-brief §4 (Teams theme is a required state) + the Entra/Teams config recipe
      in spec Dependencies. teams-app-r1 already proved host detection + Teams host adapter selecting the workforce
      strategy + MSAL v5 NAA live — R2 adopts that host; this task adds the packaging + framing + theme-bridge layer.
      The SWA framing requirement is exact: CSP frame-ancestors 'self' https://teams.microsoft.com https://*.cloud.microsoft,
      no X-Frame-Options. The Teams JS SDK init must be a no-op outside Teams.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/staticwebapp.config.json</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/host/TeamsHostAdapter.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/App.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts (useTheme/ThemeToggle)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>011 (shell scaffold — the theme bridge feeds the shell's FluentProvider; the manifest points at the built shell).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">CSP frame-ancestors MUST be exactly 'self' https://teams.microsoft.com https://*.cloud.microsoft with NO X-Frame-Options header (spec FR-04 / Dependencies recipe).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse the teams-app-r1 host detection + Teams host adapter; do not rebuild them; this task adds packaging/framing/theme only (§11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Teams theme (light/dark/high-contrast) MUST bridge to the Fluent v9 theme via semantic tokens; zero hardcoded hex; the app renders correctly in Teams dark.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Teams JS SDK init MUST be a no-op outside Teams (browser path unaffected).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/office-outlook-teams-integration-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/LEGALWORKSPACE-EMBEDDED-MODE-CONTRACT.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Teams host adapter" location="src/client/external-spa/src/host/TeamsHostAdapter.ts">detectTeamsHost :102 — reuse for theme-change subscription + no-op-outside-Teams init.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Fluent theme" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts">useTheme/ThemeToggle — the FluentProvider the Teams theme bridges into.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Author the Teams personal-tab manifest (app id, name, personal-tab contentUrl = SWA host, valid domains) per the teams-app-r1 recipe; include an icons/color set.</step>
    <step order="2">Set staticwebapp.config.json CSP frame-ancestors to 'self' https://teams.microsoft.com https://*.cloud.microsoft and ensure NO X-Frame-Options header is emitted.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the Teams theme bridge: subscribe to Teams theme changes (via TeamsHostAdapter) and map light/dark/contrast to the Fluent v9 theme fed to the shell FluentProvider; no-op outside Teams.</step>
    <step order="4">Build (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; npm run build:prod); verify zero errors and that the config is emitted in the build output.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="6">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build TS/React (build:prod)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Teams personal-tab manifest (src/client/external-spa/teams/ or equivalent)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/staticwebapp.config.json</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/ (Teams theme bridge)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the SWA config, when inspected, then CSP frame-ancestors is exactly 'self' https://teams.microsoft.com https://*.cloud.microsoft and no X-Frame-Options header is present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the app loaded in the Teams personal tab, when Teams is in dark theme, then the shell renders in dark via the Fluent v9 bridge (semantic tokens adapt; zero hardcoded hex).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the app loaded in a plain browser, when it initializes, then the Teams JS SDK init is a no-op and the browser experience is unaffected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The manifest is a personal tab pointing at the SWA content URL with valid domains for the SWA host.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Teams dark render"><steps><step>Load the app in the Teams personal tab</step><step>Set Teams to dark theme</step></steps><expected>shell renders dark via Fluent bridge; no console errors</expected></test>
    <test name="Teams high-contrast"><steps><step>Set Teams to high-contrast</step></steps><expected>Fluent high-contrast theme applied; readable</expected></test>
    <test name="Browser no-op"><steps><step>Load in a plain browser</step></steps><expected>Teams SDK init no-op; app works normally</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    Entra/Teams config recipe (pre-authorized Teams client app-ids, NAA brk-multihub:// redirect, v1 audience) is in
    spec Dependencies and is applied at the app-registration level (ops) — this task is the SWA-side manifest + framing
    + theme. The operator-gated Teams live E2E is a P1 prerequisite handled at deploy (task 019).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt; before starting; follow the task-execute pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
